<title>UK: TBI ends talks to buy Coventry airport.</title>
<headline>TBI ends talks to buy Coventry airport.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>British property and airports company TBI Plc said on Monday talks to buy Coventry airport from Coventry City Council have been terminated.</p>
<p>TBI said it had not been able to reach a &quot;mutually satisfactory&quot; agreement with Coventry City Council.</p>
<p>It announced in January it was in advanced discussions to buy the airport.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
